*   **mpg**: ecoFLEX models are designed for high efficiency. Official combined MPG figures range from 60.1 mpg (1.3 CDTi 75PS) to 74.3 mpg (1.6 CDTi 110PS). Real-world MPG is often lower, with the 1.3 CDTi ecoFLEX averaging 51.7 mpg and the 1.6 CDTi ecoFLEX averaging around 40-50 mpg in one user report, though Honest John suggests closer to 50 mpg for the 1.6. This is generally very good efficiency, especially the diesels. Score: 0.75.
*   **co2_g_km**: CO2 emissions for ecoFLEX models are low, ranging from 99 g/km to 119 g/km. The 1.6 CDTi 110PS is 105 g/km or 115 g/km. The 1.3 CDTi 95PS is 109 g/km or 119 g/km. This is relatively low compared to older cars or large engines, and excellent for a non-electric vehicle. Score: 0.75.
